{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"close","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Releases the HTTP client and its connection pool, and clears the cookie jar, the CSRF token"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and any retained "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" challenge token (§18.1 rule 6)."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Idempotent","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (rule 2): calling it twice is a no-op the second time. Cleanup code runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from error paths, and an error path that itself throws hides the original failure."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does not log out"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (rule 5): it issues no request. The server-side session deliberately"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"outlives the client object — that is what lets a process restart and resume — so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close()"},{"type":"text","text":" that logged out would silently end every user’s session on each deploy."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use after close is an error, not undefined","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (rule 4): every operation afterwards","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkError","type":"reference"},{"text":" naming the cause rather than silently reopening.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cannot ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and releasing an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncHTTPClient","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is async, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this SDK cannot make deallocation a complete shutdown the way §18.1 rule 1’s “a ","type":"text"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plus explicit ","type":"text"},{"code":"close()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"” suggests. ","type":"text"},{"code":"close()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is therefore the only complete form, and is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stated as required rather than implied.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Note"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/close()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Deterministic shutdown (CONTRACT.md §18).","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"close"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC5closeyyYaKF","title":"close()","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"symbolKind":"method"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamclient\/close()"]}],"schemaVersio